---
import ToolLayout from '../components/ToolLayout.astro';
import ResizeTool from '../tools/resize/ResizeTool';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Resize image online free: pixels, percent or KB | iDuckImg"
  description="Resize JPG, PNG and WebP by pixels or percentage, or shrink to a target file size in KB. Free, in your browser, no upload."
  heading="Resize images"
>
  <ResizeTool client:load />
  <section slot="content" class="prose mt-10">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">How to resize an image</h2>
    <ol class="mt-2 list-decimal pl-6">
      <li>Drop your JPG, PNG or WebP files, or paste them.</li>
      <li>Set a width and height in pixels, or a percentage. Leave one box empty to keep the proportions.</li>
      <li>Optionally enter a target size in KB, for example 100, and we pick the best quality that fits.</li>
      <li>Press Resize and download each file, or all of them as a ZIP.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
      A target size works for JPG and WebP. PNG is lossless, so a PNG with a target size is saved as
      WebP. If the target is too small for the chosen dimensions, you will see a message and can
      choose a smaller size.
    </p>
  </section>
</ToolLayout>
